      "provenance": {
        "cve": "CVE-2016-8619",
        "project": "curl",
        "fixCommit": "3d6460edeee21d7d790ec570d0887bed1f4366dd",
        "url": "https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/3d6460edeee21d7d790ec570d0887bed1f4366dd",
        "note": "Minimal reproduction of the curl krb5 read_data double-free: realloc(buf->data, len) with an attacker-controlled len==0 acts as free(buf->data) and returns NULL; read_data returns error without clearing buf->data, so the krb5 connection cleanup frees the field a second time. The realloc(0)=free edge is modelled as an explicit free(buf->data); state C mirrors the upstream fix (guard the realloc on a non-zero length)."
      }
